#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD0029 expect=skipped domain=LB
#note "dataset LB without the LBSTRESU column, two numeric standardised results. Requirements.Variables.All [--STRESU] gates the rule out -> auditable skip naming the absent variable, instead of one finding per record under absent = all-missing (EC-43). Both rows WOULD fire if the gate were removed, so this scenario is the discriminator for it. Aligned with the --ORRESU arm (FDA-SD0026-valid_orresu_absent-QS): the two sheets carry the same 'should not be NULL' text, so the arms no longer diverge on column absence."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col LBSTRESC type=Char label="Character Result/Finding in Std Format"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 1 | GLUC | 5.5
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 2 | ALB  | 40
